# ============================================================
# CODING STYLE RULES
# ============================================================

## 🧼 General
- No semicolons
- Use ES modules
- Simple, clean React components
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction

## 🌿 SASS
- One component → one Sass file
- Reference global variables only
- Avoid deep nesting (>3 levels)
- DRY (reuse mixins/variables)

---

# ============================================================
# WHAT NOT TO DO
# ============================================================
- Do NOT use TypeScript
- Do NOT use Tailwind
- Do NOT install UI libraries
- Do NOT add random new brand colors
- Do NOT overcomplicate animations
- Do NOT introduce complex state management
- Do NOT write magic numbers → always use variables, spacing scale
- Do NOT make it look "woo woo" or illegitimate
- Do NOT add heavy textures or busy backgrounds
- Do NOT use aggressive or bouncy animations

## GSAP Anti-Patterns (DO NOT DO):
- Do NOT use `useLayoutEffect` + `gsap.context()` manually - ALWAYS use `useGSAP()` hook instead
- Do NOT use `useEffect` for GSAP animations - use `useGSAP()` hook
- Do NOT forget to register `useGSAP` plugin - always call `gsap.registerPlugin(useGSAP)` (or include it with other plugins)
- Do NOT use `onUpdate` callbacks for animations - use timelines instead
- Do NOT manually calculate progress in ScrollTrigger callbacks - let GSAP handle it
- Do NOT create ScrollTrigger without timelines when animating - prefer `gsap.timeline({ scrollTrigger: {...} })`
- Do NOT use manual `gsap.set()` in loops for animated values - use `gsap.to()` or `gsap.from()` with stagger
- Do NOT write custom interpolation functions - use `gsap.utils.interpolate()` or let GSAP handle it
- Do NOT create multiple ScrollTriggers when one timeline can handle multiple animations
- Do NOT manually return cleanup functions - `useGSAP()` handles cleanup automatically

---

# ============================================================
# ATMOSPHERIC ELEMENTS - USE SPARINGLY
# ============================================================
Mystical elements that ARE allowed (when used subtly):
- Slow rotating geometric shapes (low opacity)
- Twinkling stars (elegant, not flashy)
- Soft radial glows behind key content
- Vignette effects to focus attention
- Subtle gradient overlays
- Particle effects (if extremely subtle)

These should enhance the professional atmosphere, not distract from it.

